    "alert_id": "ALERT_TDF_PHOSPHATE_001",
    "title": "Low phosphate with TDF — proximal tubulopathy risk",
    "message": "Guidelines list tubular wasting syndrome and renal failure as TDF adverse effects, and recommend eGFR monitoring at 3, 6, then 6–12 monthly, with additional checks in high-risk patients including those with co-existent hypertension. Patient on TDF for 6 years with serum phosphate 0.78 mmol/L, trace proteinuria, creatinine 112 umol/L, and hypertension. Hypophosphataemia is a hallmark of TDF-induced proximal tubular dysfunction. Evidence against drug attribution: occupational back pain could explain musculoskeletal symptoms, and trace proteinuria may reflect hypertensive nephropathy. However, the combination of low phosphate and proteinuria on TDF strongly suggests emerging tubulopathy. No eGFR value is documented.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Calculate eGFR. Check urine for phosphate and glucose. Consider switching TDF to TAF or alternative NRTI if tubulopathy confirmed. Monitor renal function and phosphate closely.",
