    "alert_id": "ALERT_TDF_IBUPROFEN_002",
    "title": "TDF plus NSAID increases nephrotoxicity risk",
    "message": "Guidelines note that TDF can cause renal failure and tubular wasting syndrome, and that intercurrent illness with dehydration may worsen renal function in patients on TDF. Patient uses over-the-counter ibuprofen regularly for chronic back pain while on TDF. NSAIDs reduce renal perfusion via prostaglandin inhibition, compounding TDF-related tubular injury. The patient already has low phosphate and trace proteinuria, suggesting early renal tubular involvement. This combination amplifies risk of acute kidney injury.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Minimise or avoid NSAID use in patient on TDF with evidence of tubular dysfunction. Consider non-pharmacological pain management or refer for musculoskeletal evaluation.",
