    "alert_id": "ALERT_EGFR_MISSING_003",
    "title": "eGFR not documented despite TDF and hypertension",
    "message": "Guidelines require eGFR monitoring before TDF initiation, at 3 and 6 months, then 6–12 monthly, and specify additional monitoring in high-risk patients with co-existent hypertension. Patient is on TDF with hypertension, trace proteinuria, and low phosphate, yet no eGFR is recorded. Creatinine alone (112 umol/L) does not substitute for eGFR, especially in a 51-year-old with compounding renal risk factors. The clinician's plan does not include renal function assessment.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Calculate eGFR from current creatinine. Given low phosphate and proteinuria, perform comprehensive renal monitoring including urinary phosphate and glucose.",
