    "alert_id": "ALERT_BP_CONTROL_004",
    "title": "Uncontrolled BP with TDF nephrotoxicity risk",
    "message": "Guidelines identify hypertension as a high-risk factor requiring enhanced TDF renal monitoring. Patient's BP is 146/94 with admitted amlodipine non-adherence. Uncontrolled hypertension combined with trace proteinuria may worsen renal function independently of TDF, while also increasing the threshold for detecting TDF-related tubular injury. The plan refills amlodipine without intensifying antihypertensive therapy despite confirmed suboptimal control.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Address amlodipine adherence with pill boxes or reminders. If BP remains elevated after adherence optimisation, consider dose increase or addition of a second antihypertensive agent.",
